<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pune</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Poona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pune, formerly Poona, is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-plateau">Deccan plateau</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> spent his youth there, and in the 18th century it became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> chief ministers, with their palace of Shaniwar Wada. The British took it in 1817 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-maratha-war">Third Anglo-Maratha War</a>. It later became a centre of education and social reform.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pune.jpg" alt="Pune" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ujjawal.Gayakwad · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pune_West_skyline_-_March_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
